      "role": "user",
      "content": "I see. You mentioned the high register can feel \"brittle.\" I've heard musicians talk about \"ghost notes\" or these strange, almost phantom-like qualities that appear when certain harmonics interact strangely. In a professional acoustic setting, would you describe those phenomena as mathematical anomalies in the overtone series, or is there something else at play when the sound starts to feel less stable?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
